<title>INDIA: INDIA GRAIN 97/98 WINTER CROP SEEN AT 107 MLN T.</title>
<headline>INDIA GRAIN 97/98 WINTER CROP SEEN AT 107 MLN T.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's winter foodgrain crop in fiscal 1997/98 (April-March) is forecast at 105 million tonnes to 107 million tonnes compared to 104.7 million tonnes in the same period a year ago, an independent think-tank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect kharif (winter) foodgrains production to reach 105-107 million tonnes, the Centre for Monitoring Indian Economy (CMIE) said.  </p>
<p>India also harvests a rabi, or summer, crop.</p>
<p>Total foodgrain production during 1996/97 was 198.2 million tonnes against 185.1 million tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom (91) 22-265-9000</p>
</text>
